Z||000000||malacite||10-20-2001||10:09 PM||||i am about to take on a rocker arm cover gasket replacement.<BR>i have questions. well one anyway.<P>do i have to drain the oil or coolant to remove the rocker arm cover?<BR>i don't think i have to, but i don't want to find out the hard way.<P>also, are there any matenence things i could should do while the rocker arm cover is off?<P>thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Malacite<P>Grendel-88 fiero se,  <BR>        tech 4<BR>paulie- 94 saturn sw2||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-20-2001||11:01 PM||||Whether changing the rocker gaskets on a 4 or 6 cyl, you do not need to drain any coolant or oil.  Just take the bolts off, clean off the old gasket and the surface it seals to on the head(s), and put the new gasket on and torque down the bolts.  When trying to get the cover off, try not to pry on it, or you may bend a portion of it and then it could possibly not seal very well anymore.<P>Also, looking at your sig file, how do you have an 88 SE?  To the best of my knowledge there were no SE's in 88.||||reg||1
